/-!
# A non-separated group algebraic space over a field

Every group scheme over a field is separated, but a group algebraic space over a field need
not be. Over a field of characteristic zero the quotient `𝔸¹_k/ℤ` of the affine line by the
integer translations is a group algebraic space of finite type over `Spec k` which is neither
separated, nor quasi-separated, nor locally separated over `Spec k`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Examples.NonSeparatedGroupSpace.sectionsModZ` sends a commutative ring to its
  additive group modulo the subgroup generated by the unit.
* `Stacks.Examples.NonSeparatedGroupSpace.sectionsModZSheaf` is the fppf sheafification of the
  presheaf of global sections modulo the integers on the big fppf site over `Spec k`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Examples.NonSeparatedGroupSpace.translationQuotientIsoSectionsModZSheaf` identifies
  `𝔸¹_k/ℤ` with that sheafification.
* `exists_isFiniteType_groupAlgebraicSpace_not_isSeparatedOver`, in this namespace, is
  Stacks 06EA.

## Implementation notes

The group law comes from addition of sections: the presheaf of sections modulo the integers is
a group object in presheaves of sets, and sheafification preserves finite products, hence group
objects. The failures of separation all come from the quotient not being decent, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.AffineLineTranslation.not_isDecentSpace_translationQuotient`, together with
the implications that a locally separated or quasi-separated algebraic space is decent.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 06EA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06EA)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

